<!-- ========== SUB HERO ========== -->
<section class="sub-hero">
  <div class="sub-hero-inner">
    <div class="eyebrow">— Compliance &amp; Governance</div>
    <h1>Built to satisfy the regulator, the auditor, <em>and the holder</em>.</h1>
    <p class="lead">A full overview of the legal, operational, and risk frameworks that govern every ZenX Token — and the institution that issues them.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== ENTITY & JURISDICTION ========== -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="content-block">
    <h2>Entity &amp; Jurisdiction</h2>
    <p>ZenX Limited is incorporated in the British Virgin Islands as a BVI Business Company. The Issuer's role in relation to each ZenX Token is limited to: issuing, minting, burning and administering the token; maintaining issuance and redemption records; and processing redemptions.</p>
    <ul class="list">
      <li><strong>Legal Name</strong><span>ZenX Limited</span></li>
      <li><strong>Jurisdiction</strong><span>British Virgin Islands (BVI)</span></li>
      <li><strong>Entity Type</strong><span>BVI Business Company</span></li>
      <li><strong>Governing Law</strong><span>BVI Business Company Act · BVI AML Regulations</span></li>
      <li><strong>Compliance Partners</strong><span>Licensed third-party providers for KYC / AML / Travel Rule</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>The appointment of a service provider — for custody, compliance, or technology — does not alter the rights expressly set out in the ZenX Token whitepaper and the applicable token purchase agreement.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== ISSUANCE & REDEMPTION ========== -->
<section class="section" style="background: var(--bg-card);">
  <div class="content-block">
    <h2>Issuance &amp; Redemption Mechanics</h2>

    <h3>Issuance Principles</h3>
    <p>Each ZenX Token is issued by reference to a corresponding quantity of a specified underlying asset. The underlying asset does not, in itself, constitute a security or other investment product under applicable law.</p>
    <p>A ZenX Token may be minted before the Issuer has acquired the corresponding quantity of the underlying asset, but the Issuer will subsequently acquire and hold, for its own account, such quantity — and will in any event do so before completing the redemption of that token. A ZenX Token surrendered and accepted for redemption will be burned, cancelled, or otherwise made unavailable for further use.</p>

    <h3>Issuer Redemption Undertaking</h3>
    <p>Upon valid surrender of a ZenX Token and completion of the ownership and quantity verification required to process the redemption, the Issuer undertakes to each holder that it will deliver — or arrange for the delivery of — the corresponding underlying asset, in accordance with the applicable conversion ratio and applicable law.</p>
    <p>For rFUIDL, the Issuer undertakes that each rFUIDL may be redeemed for one FUIDL on a 1:1 quantity basis. Following completion of the redemption, the corresponding rFUIDL will be burned, cancelled, or otherwise made unavailable for further use.</p>

    <h3>Exceptional Redemption</h3>
    <p>If a smart-contract failure, cyber incident, force-majeure event, or other exceptional circumstance prevents normal redemption, the holder may apply through the manual procedure specified by the Issuer and provide satisfactory evidence of ownership and quantity. Following verification and the locking, burning, cancellation, or other isolation of the relevant ZenX Tokens, the Issuer will arrange redemption of the corresponding underlying assets in accordance with the applicable conversion ratio.</p>

    <div class="quote-block">
      <p>"Holding a ZenX Token is not investment in ZenX. It is a contractual right to the underlying — and a hard undertaking to deliver."</p>
      <cite>— From the ZenX Token Whitepaper</cite>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== CUSTODY & RISK ========== -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="content-block">
    <h2>Custody, Reserves &amp; Risk</h2>

    <h3>Underlying Asset Custody</h3>
    <p>Underlying assets corresponding to issued ZenX Tokens are held by independent qualified custodians, fully segregated from ZenX Limited's own corporate balance sheet. For partner platforms such as <a href="https://realfinance.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold);">RealFinance</a>, this includes the qualified-custody arrangements coordinated for the underlying FUIDL reserves backing rFUIDL and rsFUIDL.</p>

    <h3>Reserves &amp; Attestation</h3>
    <ul class="list">
      <li><strong>Reserve Ratio</strong><span>1:1 with outstanding issued token supply</span></li>
      <li><strong>Segregation</strong><span>Underlying assets fully segregated from ZenX corporate balance sheet</span></li>
      <li><strong>Attestation</strong><span>Periodic third-party reserve attestation</span></li>
      <li><strong>Custody Standard</strong><span>Independent qualified-custodian holding</span></li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Smart-Contract &amp; Operational Risk</h3>
    <p>ZenX Tokens deployed on public chains carry smart-contract risk by nature. We mitigate this through conservative architecture, third-party audits before mainnet deployment, multi-sig administrative controls, timelocks on sensitive parameters, and an exceptional-redemption manual channel as a final-resort recovery mechanism.</p>

    <h3>Jurisdictional &amp; Sanctions Controls</h3>
    <p>In line with global RWA compliance practice, ZenX Tokens incorporate jurisdictional controls at the smart-contract, platform-frontend, and custodian-routing layers, including sanctions-list screening and address-blocking against prohibited jurisdictions.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== WHITEPAPER & AGREEMENT ========== -->
<section class="section" style="background: var(--bg-card);">
  <div class="content-block">
    <h2 id="whitepaper">Documentation</h2>
    <p>The complete legal and technical framework for ZenX Tokens is set out in the following documents. Both are Schedule 2 to the applicable Token Purchase Agreement, and should be read together with Schedule 1 (Token-Specific Terms).</p>

    <ul class="list" style="margin-top: 32px;">
      <li id="whitepaper-item">
        <strong>Whitepaper</strong>
        <span><strong>Schedule 2 — ZenX Token Whitepaper</strong> (Token-Level Description for Non-Security Analysis Purposes). Describes the general design, issuance, use, and redemption of ZenX Tokens. <em>Available under NDA upon request.</em></span>
      </li>
      <li id="agreement-item">
        <strong>Agreement</strong>
        <span><strong>Token Purchase Agreement &amp; Schedule 1 (Token-Specific Terms)</strong>. The contractual layer binding each token issuance. <em>Available under NDA upon request.</em></span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-32">To request access to either document, please <a href="contact.html" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gold);">contact us</a> with your institutional details.</p>
  </div>
</section>

